Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 04:39:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Grant every role read on the attachment vocabulary

Found by reviewing launch readiness end to end: the permission plan granted the transaction
DocTypes but not the two vocabulary tables added a moment earlier. A Link field cannot resolve a
record the user may not read, so a provisioned site would have shown a clerk an empty
attachment-type picker on a field that is required - a silent hole, because the form would look
complete.

governance_plan now folds VOCABULARY_READ into every role's plan once, so a role added later
cannot forget it. The test replays that same merge against the shipped source and asserts the
result per role, instead of reading either half on its own, and a second test holds the merge
mechanism in place.

ATTACHMENTS.md says which mechanism makes the grant: materialize for a provisioned site, Role
Permission Manager for a hand-built one.
